@startuml

title Patient Prontuary State Machine

state new {
    initial
    note right: This state represents a new prontuary that has just been initiated.
}

state pending {
    note left: The prontuary is in this state while the nurse reviews it for triaging priorities. It may be waiting for additional information or clarification.
}

state triaged {
    note top: After assessment, the prontuary is assigned a priority level based on clinical needs. This state indicates that triage has been completed.
}

state in progress {
    note bottom: The prontuary is being actively treated or managed by healthcare providers. Progress notes and updates are recorded here.
}

state complete {
    note right: The prontuary is finalized, either because the patient's condition is resolved or other disposition actions have been taken (e.g., transfer, discharge).
}

new --> pending : Review/Assessment

pending --> triaged : Triage Decision

triaged --> in progress : Treatment Initiation

in progress --> complete : Completion of Treatment/Discharge

@enduml